<title>UK: Railtrack director quits, gives no reasons.</title>
<headline>Railtrack director quits, gives no reasons.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Howell, a director of British rail network operator Railtrack Group Plc, resigned from his post on Friday, the company said.</p>
<p>The company, recently floated on the London bourse, gave no reason for his resignation.</p>
<p>His main job as head of commercial functions was to develop the company's relationships with train operating customers and interact with the office of the Rail Regulator.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
